 "version": 1,
 "name": "Tech 21 SansAmp GT2",
 "description": "Tech 21 SansAmp GT2 as traced by J. Luja (2002, Rev. 2 10-24-02) and drawn on the Tonepad 'Sin Amp 2' schematic (Rev. 2, Jan 24 2003). IC1a buffer and IC1b x5.5 stage share the input node -> AMP switch S3 picks the Drive feed (California C20 .01 / British C25 .0022 from IC1b, Tweed: the C19/C24/C26 + R36 network from the buffer) and IC2a's gain leg (R37, or R37 // R38) -> Drive 100 kB -> IC2a (330 k // 220 p) -> IC2b (330 k // 220 p, MOD switch S2 bank A sets its leg: R29 10 k, or R29 // R24 1 k) -> two Sallen-Key low-pass followers (IC3a ~3 kHz Q ~2 with the R5/C7 shelf, IC3b ~3.2 kHz) -> S2 bank B (Hot Wired through C18 .01, Hi Gain through R30 10 k, Clean direct) -> node Z with R35 to VB and R34 to the Level top -> MIC switch S1 (C17/C23 .0047, C22 .022, R23 6.2 k, R22 22 k) -> Level 100 kB -> IC4a x3.3 -> Baxandall High/Low around IC4b -> NPN emitter-follower output. There are no clipping diodes: the op-amps clip at their rails. Switch throws to positions: Luja's pin labels (poles 3 and 6; throws 1/2/4 and 8/7/5) with the Tonepad schematic's explicit position drawing (position 1 = throws 1 and 8, 2 = 2 and 7, 3 = 4 and 5). Engine note: the rail-clipping IC2b group runs at 8x a 48 kHz host (see multirate).",
 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "Tech 21 SansAmp GT-2 traced schematic, drawn by J. Luja 2002, Rev. 2 10-24-02 (all values, the three 2-pole 3-throw switch banks by pin number, the switch legends)",
   "url": "https://schematicsonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Tech-21-SansAmp-GT-2.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "Tonepad 'Sin Amp 2' (SansAmp GT2) schematic and layout, Francisco Pena, Rev. 2 Jan 24 2003: the same values, every switch throw drawn by position (S1A/S1B, S2A/S2B, S3A/S3B, positions 1-3), parts list 4 x TL072 + BC413B",
   "url": "https://www.pisotones.com/GT2/GT2.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "Tech 21 SansAmp GT2 owner's manual (Rev 5/06): switch legends and what each position does; 1 Mohm input",
   "url": "https://www.tech21nyc.com/t21manuals/GT2-OM.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "GroupDIY, 'Sans amp GT2 from tonepad': the Tonepad switch wiring (S?A0/S?B0 common, 1-3 positions), and the observation that MIC positions 1 and 2 look the same in the circuit",
   "url": "https://groupdiy.com/threads/sans-amp-gt2-from-tonepad.12684/"
  }
 ],
 "io": {
  "input": "in",
  "output": "out",
  "inputVoltsPerFS": 1.0,
  "outputVoltsPerFS": 1.0
 },
 "oversampling": 8,
 "newton": {"groups": {"IC2B": 5e-05}},
 "solver": "auto",
 "multirate": {
  "rates": {
   "IC2B": 32
  },
  "events": true,
  "note": "Base 384 kHz (oversampling 8, was 2), IC2b's group with events at 32: 4 substeps (1.536 MHz) on every LTE event (docs §10.48, §10.63). IC2b (x175 in Hot Wired / Hi Gain) clips at its rails; that group is the whole path up to the Level amp. Was: base 96 kHz with this group on the ladder at 384 kHz: 3130 Hz gate tone (every bin) -62.8 / -59.2 / -52.5 dB at 0.25 / 0.5 / 1.0 FS (384 kHz folds), 2900 Hz -56.4 / -61.8 / -52.8; now -72.9 / -72.5 / -67.2 and -72.2 / -70.4 / -65.6. The group on the ladder at 768 kHz passes too (-67.8 worst) but is further from the truth (ngspice out 0.129 -> 0.134 %: the converters' phase); 2 substeps fail (-58.7). ngspice T/32 truth, audio band: 0.129 -> 0.035 %; engine T/32 truth lead / rock DI 0.128 / 0.401 -> 0.035 / 0.114 %. 9900X real / driven: 21.9 / 26.7 -> 31.5 / 36.0 % of a core."
 },
 "models": {
  "TL072": {
   "kind": "opamp",
   "level": 1,
   "a0": 200000.0,
   "gbw": 3000000.0,
   "slew": 13000000.0,
   "swing_hi": 1.5,
   "swing_lo": 1.5,
   "vhi": 9.0,
   "vlo": 0.0,
   "note": "TI TL072 (Tonepad parts list: 4 x TL072): Avd 200 V/mV, GBW 3 MHz, SR 13 V/us typ; single 9 V supply, output swing 1.5 V from each rail (datasheet VOM +/-13.5 V at +/-15 V, 10 kohm). unverified: the original GT2 board's op-amp type is not marked on the Luja trace; the input common-mode limit near the negative rail is not modelled"
  },
  "BC413B": {
   "kind": "npn",
   "is": 2e-14,
   "bf": 330.0,
   "br": 3.0,
   "note": "BC413B low-noise NPN (Tonepad parts list; the Luja trace leaves the output transistor unmarked): hFE B rank 240-500, BF 330; IS approximate. unverified: no vendor card"
  }
 },
